# stories-compute

Storybook demos for the compute service: processes spawned locally and on EDGE through one
`Process.Manager`, each rendered as a card in a masonry.

test QA-1: Prompt background agents locally and on EDGE
  desc: |
    The AgentManager story: each prompt spawns the scripted agent demo process (no model involved),
    whose card streams a read-only transcript of its plan, tool calls, tool results and answer. The
    same prompt box spawns locally or on EDGE; the card's location row is the only difference.
  actors: human
  status: verified
  given:
    - storybook serves `stories/stories-compute/AgentManager` `EdgeLocal`
    - a local EDGE stack listens on :8787 and its compute-service hosts `org.dxos.stories.compute.agent-demo`
  steps:
    - name: Prompt a local agent
      do: Type "Fix the flaky timeout in the sync engine tests" in the prompt box and press Enter.
      expect: a card appears with location "local", and its transcript shows the prompt followed by tool calls such as grep_repo and run_tests.
    - name: Prompt a second local agent
      do: Click the "Research the history of the Lisbon tram network" suggestion and press Create.
      expect: a second local card streams search_web and fetch_page calls alongside the first.
    - name: Switch to EDGE
      do: Choose EDGE in the location select.
      expect: the select reads EDGE.
    - name: Prompt an EDGE agent
      do: Type "Analyze last quarter sales by region and chart the trend" and press Enter.
      expect: a card appears with location "edge", and its transcript streams query_database, run_python and create_chart.
    - name: Prompt a second EDGE agent
      do: Type "Schedule a design review with the platform team next week" and press Enter.
      expect: a second EDGE card streams find_contacts, list_calendar and draft_email.
    - name: Let every agent finish
      do: Wait for all four transcripts to end.
      expect: every card ends with an answer and its state reads SUCCEEDED; the delete action replaces Kill.

test QA-2: Grant agents permissions and watch the guard admit or refuse their tools
  desc: |
    The Permissions story: a configurator spawns an agent on a real model (through the EDGE AI service)
    whose process holds a guard with grants for exactly the ticked permissions. Its tools are copies of
    plugin-space's queryObjects, getObjects and updateObject that declare /space/read and /space/write,
    and a sandboxExec stand-in that declares /sandbox/exec. A tool call the grants do not cover dies
    with OperationDeniedError before its handler runs; the agent sees the refusal as its tool result.
  actors: human
  status: verified
  given:
    - storybook serves `stories/stories-compute/Permissions` `Edge`
    - the space holds the organizations Acme Robotics (prospect), Bramble Coffee Roasters and Lisbon Tram Company
    - dev EDGE hosts the agent process, and preview.dxos.network/ai answers the model
  steps:
    - name: Grant Database read and list the organizations
      do: Tick only Database read, click the "List the organizations in the database." suggestion and click Spawn agent.
      expect: an "Agent 1 · local" card shows a Query Objects call, the three organizations in the answer, and a queryObjects process that SUCCEEDED.
    - name: Ask the read-only agent to write
      do: With the same grant, click the "Mark Acme Robotics as an active customer." suggestion and click Spawn agent.
      expect: |
        Agent 2's queryObjects SUCCEEDED and its updateObject process FAILED; the card reads "updateObject refused,
        denied: no grant covers the subject and command", and the agent's reply says it lacks write permission.
    - name: Run a sandbox command without Sandbox exec
      do: Click the "Run `uname -a` in the sandbox." suggestion and click Spawn agent.
      expect: Agent 3's sandboxExec process FAILED with the same denial, and the agent says it cannot run the command.
    - name: Grant Sandbox exec and run it again
      do: Tick Sandbox exec, keep the sandbox suggestion, and click Spawn agent.
      expect: Agent 4's sandboxExec process SUCCEEDED and its reply quotes the stand-in's uname output.
    - name: Ask a read-only agent on EDGE to write
      do: Untick Sandbox exec, choose EDGE in the location select, click the "Mark Acme Robotics as an active customer." suggestion and click Spawn agent.
      expect: |
        an "Agent 5 · edge" card warns "No guard on EDGE: these grants are not enforced"; its Update Object call
        succeeds and the agent reports Acme Robotics as active, although only Database read was granted.
      note: |
        Observed, not designed: RemoteProcessManager.spawn does not send SpawnOptions.guard, and deployed EDGE
        runs published @dxos packages that predate the guard check, with its own undeclared copies of the
        database operations. The sandboxExec stand-in is story-local, so an EDGE agent has no such tool.
    - name: Compare the agents
      do: Look at the five cards side by side.
      expect: local agents held exactly their grants (passes and refusals as above); the EDGE agent was not checked.
